import GroupApproximation.GGT.DGOWindmillQuasiconvex
import GroupApproximation.GGT.DGOWindmillRotationFree

/-!
# Windmills

Fourth module of the campaign aimed at
`Manuscript.NonMF.TheoremCDebts.dgoTheorem53` (DGO's Theorem 5.3(b)).

Dahmani-Guirardel-Osin, Definition 5.11.  A *windmill* for a `ρ`-separated very
rotating family is a subset `W ⊆ X` that the induction proving Theorem 5.3 can
grow: quasiconvex with a constant independent of the stage, containing at least
one apex, staying far from the apices it does not contain, invariant under the
group its apices generate, and satisfying the theorem's own conclusion for that
group.

## Three of DGO's five axioms are not recorded, and why

DGO's Definition 5.11 has five clauses.  Two of them are not carried here.

* **The free product clause** (their axiom 4, `G_W = ∗_{c ∈ S_W} G_c`) belongs to
  Theorem 5.3(a), which `GGT/HullSCDGO.lean`'s provenance audit establishes is
  *not* recorded in `HullSC.RotatingQuotient` and must not be added.  Nothing in
  the proof of 5.3(b) consumes it: the Bass-Serre tree of the growth step is
  built from `G_W` and the new rotation subgroups whatever `G_W` is, and this
  campaign replaces that tree by an induction on words in any case.
* **The shortening pair** in their axiom 5 exists to feed their Lemmas 5.18 and
  5.19, whose only role is to promote "one geodesic passes through these apices"
  to "every geodesic does".  `DGOWindmill.exists_close_of_geodesic_same_endpoints`
  does that promotion for `3δ`, so the shortening pairs are dropped along with
  5.18 and 5.19.  They are needed for DGO's §5.1.3 Greendlinger lemmas, which
  this debt does not ask for.
* **The invariant geodesic line** of their axiom 5 is replaced by
  `HullGeometry.IsLoxodromic` at a single basepoint.  That is the conclusion
  `HullSC.RotatingQuotient` asks for, it survives conjugation in one line, and it
  removes the obligation to build a bi-infinite geodesic and prove it lies inside
  `W`.  It has to carry `IsLoxodromic`'s additive constant rather than a bare
  `ρ n` bound: the broken-path induction measures displacement from the first
  apex of the word, so moving to a fixed basepoint costs a constant.

## The constants are re-derived, not transcribed

`HullGeometry.IsHyperbolicSpace δ` is the four-point condition, whose triangles
are `3δ`-thin.  So `quasiconvex` asks for `6δ` where DGO ask for `4δ`, and `far`
asks for `55δ` where DGO ask for `50δ`.  The growth step's budget, checked
end to end before any of this was written, is: new apices are collected out to
`75δ`, the unfolded windmill is `15δ`-quasiconvex, and `W' = W₂^{+15δ}`, which
leaves apices outside `W'` at distance at least `75δ - 15δ = 60δ`, clearing the
`55δ` that `far` demands.

## Model tests

Every clause was checked against three models before the structure was written.

* `X = ℝ`, `C = 200δ·ℤ`, `Rot c` the order-two reflection at `c`, and
  `W = [-100δ, 100δ]`.  All five hypotheses of Theorem 5.3 hold there and the
  family is genuinely very rotating rather than vacuously so; the group the
  rotations generate is infinite dihedral, and its elements are the reflections
  at apices and the translations by `400δ·ℤ`.  Every clause below holds for
  that `W`, and the conclusion of Theorem 5.3(b) is true in the model.
* The one-point space of `GGT/DGORotatingQuotientRefutation.lean` -- the model
  that refutes the statements this debt used to carry.  `W = univ` is a windmill
  there: `far` is vacuous and `dichotomy` holds because the windmill group is
  `Rot pt`.  So the structure is **not** contradictory at the configuration that
  killed its predecessors.
* `C = ∅`: no windmill exists, `apex_mem` failing.  That is correct and
  deliberate -- `HullSC.not_rotation_or_loxodromic_of_empty` refutes the
  unrestricted dichotomy exactly there, so the empty family has to be discharged
  outside this machinery, from `HullSC.rotationNormalClosure_empty`.

The third test is also why `dichotomy` may be stated for *every* element of the
windmill group including `1`, where the top-level statement may not: `apex_mem`
supplies an apex of `W`, and `1` lies in its rotation subgroup.
-/

namespace GroupApproximation
namespace DGOWindmill

open GroupApproximation.HullGeometry
open GroupApproximation.HullSC

universe u v

variable {G : Type u} [Group G] {X : Type v} [PseudoMetricSpace X]
  [MulAction G X]

/-! ## The group of a windmill -/

/-- **The subgroup generated by the rotations at the apices inside `W`.**  DGO
write `G_W`. -/
def windmillGroup (C : Set X) (Rot : X → Subgroup G) (W : Set X) : Subgroup G :=
  Subgroup.closure {g : G | ∃ c ∈ C, c ∈ W ∧ g ∈ Rot c}

omit [PseudoMetricSpace X] [MulAction G X] in
theorem mem_windmillGroup {C : Set X} {Rot : X → Subgroup G} {W : Set X}
    {c : X} (hc : c ∈ C) (hcW : c ∈ W) {g : G} (hg : g ∈ Rot c) :
    g ∈ windmillGroup C Rot W :=
  Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨c, hc, hcW, hg⟩

omit [PseudoMetricSpace X] [MulAction G X] in
/-- **`G_W` is the smallest subgroup containing every rotation at an apex of
`W`.**  The elimination principle for `windmillGroup`, used wherever an element
of it has to be shown to preserve something. -/
theorem windmillGroup_le {C : Set X} {Rot : X → Subgroup G} {W : Set X}
    {H : Subgroup G} (h : ∀ c ∈ C, c ∈ W → Rot c ≤ H) :
    windmillGroup C Rot W ≤ H := by
  show Subgroup.closure {g : G | ∃ c ∈ C, c ∈ W ∧ g ∈ Rot c} ≤ H
  rw [Subgroup.closure_le]
  intro g hg
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hcW, hgr⟩ := hg
  exact h c hc hcW hgr

theorem windmillGroup_mono {C : Set X} {Rot : X → Subgroup G} {W W' : Set X}
    (hWW : W ⊆ W') : windmillGroup C Rot W ≤ windmillGroup C Rot W' := by
  refine windmillGroup_le ?_
  intro c hc hcW
  rw [SetLike.le_def]
  intro g hg
  exact mem_windmillGroup hc (hWW hcW) hg

/-- Every rotation at an apex of `W` lies in the subgroup the rotations
generate, so `G_W` is contained in the whole rotation closure. -/
theorem windmillGroup_le_rotationNormalClosure {C : Set X}
    {Rot : X → Subgroup G} (W : Set X) :
    windmillGroup C Rot W ≤ rotationNormalClosure C Rot := by
  refine windmillGroup_le ?_
  intro c hc _
  rw [SetLike.le_def]
  intro g hg
  exact mem_rotationNormalClosure hc hg

/-! ## Windmills -/

/-- **A windmill** (DGO, Definition 5.11), in the form the proof of Theorem
5.3(b) needs.  See the module header for the three clauses of DGO's definition
that are deliberately absent and for the model tests each clause was checked
against.

`dichotomy` is the theorem's own conclusion, restricted to `G_W`: the induction
proves it for a growing sequence of windmills whose union of groups is the whole
rotation closure.

The separation constant `ρ` is **not** a parameter: no clause mentions it.  It
enters the growth step as a hypothesis, alongside `200δ ≤ ρ`, and the
`IsSeparated` of the ambient family; a windmill itself is a purely metric
object. -/
structure IsWindmill (G : Type u) (X : Type v) [Group G] [PseudoMetricSpace X]
    [MulAction G X] (δ : ℝ) (C : Set X) (Rot : X → Subgroup G) (W : Set X) :
    Prop where
  /-- `W` is `6δ`-quasiconvex.  DGO ask for `4δ`; the four-point condition costs
  `6δ`. -/
  quasiconvex : IsQuasiconvexSet W (6 * δ)
  /-- `W` contains an apex.  Without this the windmill group can be trivial and
  `dichotomy` fails at `1`. -/
  apex_mem : ∃ c ∈ C, c ∈ W
  /-- Every apex outside `W` is `55δ` from every point of `W`.  DGO's
  `W^{+50δ} ∩ C = W ∩ C`, stated pointwise so that no infimum has to be
  unfolded. -/
  far : ∀ c ∈ C, c ∉ W → ∀ w ∈ W, 55 * δ ≤ dist c w
  /-- `G_W` preserves `W`. -/
  invariant : ∀ g ∈ windmillGroup C Rot W, ∀ w ∈ W, g • w ∈ W
  /-- Theorem 5.3(b) for `G_W`: every element is a rotation at an apex of `W`,
  or is loxodromic.

  The loxodromic branch is existential in the basepoint because that is what the
  broken-path induction produces -- a displacement bound measured from the first
  apex of the word, with an additive constant.  `isLoxodromic_of_isLoxodromic`
  moves it to every basepoint, which is the form
  `HullSC.RotatingQuotient.rotation_or_loxodromic` records. -/
  dichotomy : ∀ g ∈ windmillGroup C Rot W,
    (∃ c ∈ C, c ∈ W ∧ g ∈ Rot c) ∨ (∃ x : X, IsLoxodromic g x)

/-! ## The apices inside a windmill are the ones its group rotates about -/

/-- **An apex within `55δ` of a windmill is inside it.**  The contrapositive of
`far`, in the form the growth step consumes. -/
theorem mem_of_dist_lt_of_isWindmill {δ : ℝ} {C : Set X}
    {Rot : X → Subgroup G} {W : Set X}
    (hW : IsWindmill G X δ C Rot W) {c : X} (hc : c ∈ C) {w : X} (hw : w ∈ W)
    (hlt : dist c w < 55 * δ) : c ∈ W := by
  by_contra hnot
  exact absurd (hW.far c hc hnot w hw) (not_le.mpr hlt)

/-! ## The base case -/

/-- **The apices of a small ball about an apex are that apex alone.**  Two
distinct apices are `ρ ≥ 200δ` apart, and the ball has radius `100δ`. -/
theorem eq_of_mem_closedBall_of_isSeparated {δ ρ : ℝ} (hδ : 0 < δ)
    (hρ : 200 * δ ≤ ρ) {C : Set X} (hsep : IsSeparated C ρ) {c₀ : X}
    (hc₀ : c₀ ∈ C) {c : X} (hc : c ∈ C)
    (hmem : c ∈ Metric.closedBall c₀ (100 * δ)) : c = c₀ := by
  refine eq_of_dist_lt_of_isSeparated hsep hc hc₀ ?_
  have h : dist c c₀ ≤ 100 * δ := Metric.mem_closedBall.mp hmem
  linarith

/-- **The windmill group of the base ball is the rotation subgroup of its
centre.** -/
theorem windmillGroup_closedBall_le {δ ρ : ℝ} (hδ : 0 < δ) (hρ : 200 * δ ≤ ρ)
    {C : Set X} {Rot : X → Subgroup G} (hsep : IsSeparated C ρ) {c₀ : X}
    (hc₀ : c₀ ∈ C) :
    windmillGroup C Rot (Metric.closedBall c₀ (100 * δ)) ≤ Rot c₀ := by
  refine windmillGroup_le ?_
  intro c hc hcW
  have hcc : c = c₀ := eq_of_mem_closedBall_of_isSeparated hδ hρ hsep hc₀ hc hcW
  exact le_of_eq (congrArg Rot hcc)

/-- **DGO's base case: the ball of radius `100δ` about an apex is a windmill.**

`quasiconvex` is `isQuasiconvexSet_closedBall` weakened from `2δ` to `6δ`;
`apex_mem` is the centre; `far` holds because an apex outside the ball is at
least `ρ ≥ 200δ` from the centre and every point of the ball is within `100δ`
of it, leaving `100δ ≥ 55δ`; `invariant` and `dichotomy` both come from
`windmillGroup_closedBall_le`, a rotation about `c₀` preserving the distance to
`c₀`. -/
theorem isWindmill_closedBall {δ ρ : ℝ} (hδ : 0 < δ) (hρ : 200 * δ ≤ ρ)
    (hhyp : IsHyperbolicSpace δ X) (hgeo : IsGeodesicSpace X) {C : Set X}
    {Rot : X → Subgroup G} (hfam : IsRotatingFamily G X C Rot)
    (hsep : IsSeparated C ρ) {c₀ : X} (hc₀ : c₀ ∈ C) :
    IsWindmill G X δ C Rot (Metric.closedBall c₀ (100 * δ)) where
  quasiconvex :=
    IsQuasiconvexSet.mono
      (isQuasiconvexSet_closedBall hhyp (le_of_lt hδ) hgeo c₀ (100 * δ))
      (by linarith)
  apex_mem := ⟨c₀, hc₀, Metric.mem_closedBall_self (by linarith)⟩
  far := by
    intro c hc hnot w hw
    have hne : c ≠ c₀ := by
      intro heq
      apply hnot
      rw [heq]
      exact Metric.mem_closedBall_self (by linarith)
    have hsepc : ρ ≤ dist c c₀ := hsep c hc c₀ hc₀ hne
    have hwc : dist w c₀ ≤ 100 * δ := Metric.mem_closedBall.mp hw
    have htri : dist c c₀ ≤ dist c w + dist w c₀ := dist_triangle c w c₀
    linarith
  invariant := by
    intro g hg w hw
    have hgr : g ∈ Rot c₀ := windmillGroup_closedBall_le hδ hρ hsep hc₀ hg
    have hwc : dist w c₀ ≤ 100 * δ := Metric.mem_closedBall.mp hw
    refine Metric.mem_closedBall.mpr ?_
    rw [dist_smul_apex_eq hfam hc₀ hgr w]
    exact hwc
  dichotomy := by
    intro g hg
    exact Or.inl ⟨c₀, hc₀, Metric.mem_closedBall_self (by linarith),
      windmillGroup_closedBall_le hδ hρ hsep hc₀ hg⟩

end DGOWindmill
end GroupApproximation
